implementation_notes:
API sketch: 
function parseStreamTo<T>(stream: ReadableStream, schema: ZodType<T>, options?: { tolerateMissingDiscriminator?: boolean }): AsyncGenerator<{value?: T, recoveryHints?: string[]}, void, void>

- The generator yields partial validated values where possible and a final object at stream end.
- 'recoveryHints' is an array of short codes (e.g., 'missing_tag', 'ambiguous_enum', 'extra_props') that callers can map to actions.

Typegen change: add an optional metadata field on unions: 
  union: { discriminator?: string, tagValues?: Record<string,string> }

Zod <-> JSON Schema helper example: 
const z = zodFromJsonSchema(schema);
const json = jsonSchemaFromZod(zodSchema);
Notes: custom Zod refinements will be emitted as 'x-zod-refinement' extension on JSON Schema and ignored on roundtrip.
